<DocsLayout title="Verification — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Verification</h1>
    <p class="lede">Use the target repository’s required checks and explicit review requirements. Every result describes the actual candidate inspected; publication and merge follow the user’s authority.</p>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Finish with evidence</h2>
<div class="grid3"><div><div class="n">1</div><div class="t">Check</div><div class="d">Run required project checks and inspect output and exit status.</div></div><div><div class="n">2</div><div class="t">Review</div><div class="d">Resolve findings on a stable candidate and refresh affected evidence after edits.</div></div><div><div class="n">3</div><div class="t">Deliver</div><div class="d">Report results, limitations, and only the publication actually authorized.</div></div></div><p>Freeze the relevant inputs during tests and review. A commit SHA alone does not identify dirty or untracked content. Record commands, candidate identity, output, and missing results. Cancellation does not satisfy a required check.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Native acceptance</h2>
<p>Authenticated native acceptance remains unrun in the API development conversation because it has no HC terminal identity. Static instruction checks, CLI observations, and offline fixtures cannot prove native end-to-end behavior.</p><p>Qualification must demonstrate native parentage, test success and failure notifications, an explicitly sent reviewer report, correction and re-review, helper questions, interruption recovery, and conservative cleanup.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/ACCEPTANCE.md")}> Acceptance matrix ↗</a> <a href={repoBlob("docs/verification/issue-348.md")}> Actual evidence and limitations ↗</a></p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Portable repository verification</h2>
<p>A project-root <code>VERIFY.md</code> describes that project’s checks. This repository’s optional development and evidence tools work independently of ordinary Sum startup.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("VERIFY.md")}> Repository verification contract ↗</a> <a href={repoBlob("skills/sum-finish/SKILL.md")}> Finish procedure ↗</a></p>
</div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
